A||N||7||1986 Fiero||Check Engine light coming on???||||1||
Z||000000||1986 Fiero||03-28-2001||12:29 PM||||My check engine light just started coming on and while its on the car lacks power very bad then it will get power and take off...but if i stop the car put it in park and shut it off then start it again (sometimes)the light goes back off and the car runs fine.Is there trouble codes equiped with the fiero,or what could be wrong?<BR>                  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-28-2001||12:46 PM||||Remove the cover where the cig lighter is.<BR>There is a connctor next to the lighter socket. take a paper clip or wire and connect the 2 top left pins (as you look at it) Next turn the ignition on to Run (don't start the car) the check engine light will flash. It should flash once then pause then flash twice. This is code 12. it is normal. It will flash the same code 3 times. Once code 12 has flashed it will then flash any error codes stored. They are all 2 digit codes. Example three flashes pause then two flashes is code 32. It will flash the error code 3 times. When it starts flashing 12 again all codes have been displayed. Turn off ignition and remove wire. Once you have the code number, post it and we can give you places to look at to correct it. Also Chilton's. Haynes, and the factory service manual can tell you what the codes mean.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-28-2001||12:47 PM||||I'm not an expert on the codes, but there is a search at the top right of the page. There are many posts on this topic with lots of info. Use codes, check engine, trouble codes as the search word.<P>You will get all the info you need.<BR>Here's one link:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005404.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005404.html</A> <P>Hope this helps<P><BR>DXR_DAD<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000003||sqoach||03-28-2001||03:03 PM||||oreif, are you sure it's the two top pins? i thought it was the bottom ones. now i gotta go check...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||03-28-2001||03:30 PM||||Just to make sure everyone is on the same page, the way I understand it is if you are facing the plug (facing rearward) your ground the 2 on the top left.  Correct me if I'm wrong.  That'll look different if you're sitting in the car, facing forward, and just look down at the plug.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000005||Hank is Here||03-28-2001||03:34 PM||||I remember it being the two pins on the top towards the passengers side.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RacinRob||03-28-2001||07:39 PM||||On my 85 GT, I just looked at the plug and there were only two pins that had little copper things in them right next to each other on the horizontal plane.  this my be different on the '86 but that is how I figured it out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Homer||03-28-2001||08:11 PM||||code 12 is just the code to tell you that everything in the ECM is operating correctly then it will flash your trouble codes...#32 has to do with the EGR system..."replace the EGR Valve"<BR>||||reg||1
